II. The pile
   
7. Landingzone for Validation / complaint ideas
    - manifest resolver must check if fileset is declared in pud_cfg with fallback to shared_cfg
        - so shared_cfg can declare defaults for it, which the pud_cfg can override
        - if not present, then complain
    - MD asset collision, fallback and absense
        - Files of Filelist, subject to the md resolver, referenced by name in Filelists, must follow these rules
            - there can be no pud internal or shared internal naming collisions
                - <pud>/onepath/file.txt and <pud>/another/file.txt is a violation
                    - because name is the same, it is pud internal collision. the same rule applies to shared internals
                - <pud>/onepath/file.txt and <shared>/another/file.txt is OK
                    - this is fine. the system uses fallback from pud to shared
        - so we need to validate that the files mentioned
            - exist in one or both repos
            - but are unique internally in any repo they exist
        - then manifest resolver can do less work

