[TESTING]: 
Assert type tests:
needs happy path testing
- ensure 'the buttons work', so dogfooding can continue (even if minor regressions)
needs to provide security from destructive actions the app may take
- ensure clankerize fails in all situations where there is a whiff of 'something we would create exists'
DX for test writing
- the class/method/atomic tests system is just nametagging the atomic test
- this is fine, but perhaps it can be less 'involved'? or it could be like it is (but then need to prevent test classes with same name overwriting)
- just better fluent api of the shadowed things.
- the UI report should be more to the point, while the json report contain the full info (no ui dumps in console, but in the report)
Import verification
- thinks 'from app.xxx import yyy' is equal to 'from app import yyy'
- needs to ban adapters from using the stdlib import, so mandate them having free reins
- needs to treat all __init__ files differently, validating that they are economical (not from bottom)
- needs to not gaf about ex 
- needs to also work the bottom level files
- output format too, but less important



goals (sticky)
1. all classes instantiated in assert methods should have a shadow, so the reader can work in that file without investigating the other files of test system
2. the console output should not be verbose, dropping big complaints on the user. instead the reports should contain the 'visibility' stuff (complete ui render | list of observed paths, etc)
3. the reports should do a great job in laying out the case, they dont quite do that now

